.TH WARM 1 "" "local-models"
.SH NAME
warm \- keep a model loaded so q answers instantly, and say when it unloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B warm
on|off|status [tier|model] [time]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keep a model loaded so q answers instantly, and say when it unloads.
.PP
Input: on, off, status or restart; a tier or model; a duration such as 1h30m.
.PP
Output: what is loaded and when it unloads; status \-\-json is the machine view.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B warm on 1h
Keep the small model loaded for an hour.
.TP
.B warm on code 4h
Keep the coding model loaded for a long session.
.TP
.B warm status
What is loaded and when it unloads.
.TP
.B warm status \-\-json
The machine view: what is loaded and when each model expires.
.TP
.B warm off
Unload the small model and give the memory back.
.TP
.B warm off all
Back to zero memory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The work ran and failed, or a check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage: unknown flag, missing value, unknown verb.
.TP
.B 10
Server down or a backend call failed.
.TP
.B 11
Model or backend not available.
.TP
.B 12
Input missing or unreadable (file, image, history entry, optional dependency).
.TP
.B 13
Wall\-clock timeout.
.TP
.B 127
A required program is not installed.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled by the caller.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B logs/*\-history.jsonl
One JSON line per call. History is per terminal by default; \-\-all or LM_ALL=1 reaches every caller.
.SH SEE ALSO
lm(1), q(1), see(1), imagine, review
